{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:pet-ch1-left-invariant-metric","title":"def:pet-ch1-left-invariant-metric","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics.md","line":260,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics.tex#def:pet-ch1-left-invariant-metric","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:pet-ch1-riemannian-isometry]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics.tex","label":"def:pet-ch1-left-invariant-metric","line":489,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Left-invariant metric]\n  \\label{def:pet-ch1-left-invariant-metric}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0029}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch1-riemannian-isometry}\n\n  Left translation identifies $TG\\simeq G\\times T_eG$. Every inner product on\n  $T_eG$ therefore extends uniquely to a metric for which all left translations\n  are isometries; these are precisely the \\emph{left-invariant metrics} on $G$.\n  Different inner products can produce nonisometric metrics.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Left-invariant metric] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a7065742d6368312d6c6566742d696e76617269616e742d6d6574726963\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0029</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_RiemannianMetrics%23def%3Apet-ch1-riemannian-isometry\">↗ def:pet-ch1-riemannian-isometry</a> <p></p>Left translation identifies <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$TG\\simeq G\\times T_eG$\">$TG\\simeq G\\times T_eG$</span>. Every inner product on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T_eG$\">$T_eG$</span> therefore extends uniquely to a metric for which all left translations are isometries; these are precisely the <em>left-invariant metrics</em> on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$G$\">$G$</span>. Different inner products can produce nonisometric metrics. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#ex:pet-ch1-isometry-group-hyperbolic","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#rem:pet-ch1-quotient-submersion","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:pet-ch1-riemannian-isometry","title":"def:pet-ch1-riemannian-isometry","label":"def:pet-ch1-riemannian-isometry"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#rem:pet-ch1-quotient-submersion","title":"rem:pet-ch1-quotient-submersion","label":"rem:pet-ch1-quotient-submersion"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#ex:pet-ch1-su2-berger","title":"ex:pet-ch1-su2-berger","label":"ex:pet-ch1-su2-berger"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#ex:pet-ch1-left-invariant-coframe","title":"ex:pet-ch1-left-invariant-coframe","label":"ex:pet-ch1-left-invariant-coframe"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#rem:pet-ch1-ex-24","title":"rem:pet-ch1-ex-24","label":"rem:pet-ch1-ex-24"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#rem:pet-ch1-ex-25","title":"rem:pet-ch1-ex-25","label":"rem:pet-ch1-ex-25"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#rem:pet-ch1-ex-27","title":"rem:pet-ch1-ex-27","label":"rem:pet-ch1-ex-27"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#rem:pet-ch1-ex-28","tit